  "author": "Canonical Ltd.",
  "timestamp": "2026-06-25T10:46:10.839708Z",
  "version": 4,
  "statements": [
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-5895-1",
        "name": "USN-5895-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that MPlayer could be made to divide by zero when processing certain malformed media files. If a user were tricked into opening a specially crafted media file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause MPlayer to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2022-38850, CVE-2022-38860, CVE-2022-38865)  It was discovered that MPlayer could be made to read out of bounds when processing certain malformed media files. If a user were tricked into opening a specially crafted media file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause MPlayer to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2022-38851)  It was discovered that MPlayer could be made to write out of bounds when processing certain malformed media files. If a user were tricked into opening a specially crafted media file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause MPlayer to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2022-38855, CVE-2022-38858, CVE-2022-38863, CVE-2022-38864, CVE-2022-38866)  It was discovered that MPlayer did not properly managed memory when processing certain malformed media files. If a user were tricked into opening a specially crafted media file, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause MPlayer to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2022-38861)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2022-38850",
          "CVE-2022-38851",
          "CVE-2022-38855",
          "CVE-2022-38858",
          "CVE-2022-38860",
          "CVE-2022-38861",
          "CVE-2022-38863",
          "CVE-2022-38864",
          "CVE-2022-38865",
          "CVE-2022-38866"
        ]
      },
